<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I96614580a49fa39c51a8ee294d617a809793a995" commit="a562d80d332e5467c3ce41000429c7cfb5be77f1" commit_message="pygpt: Support 4K block images.  pygpt is a general disk image partition parser, we have to deal with images that use non-512b blocks. Today the major format are either 512 or 4k, so the pygpt will try to read GPT in 4k location and change block size calculation to that if needed.  This is tested by scsi_debug kernel module:  sudo modprobe scsi_debug dev_size_mb=16384 sector_size=4096 sudo lsblk -o NAME,PHY-SEC,LOG-SEC # Find the entry with NAME,4096,4096 sudo parted /dev/sdX  mktable GPT  mkpart  Start=64,END=128  sudo pygpt.py show /dev/sdX  # show information properly.  BUG=chromium:832160 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I96614580a49fa39c51a8ee294d617a809793a995 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1011903 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="10" gerrit_number="1011903" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/03/1011903/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="11"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7f1f3ad009546b9aca4dfaa72c658fdea5887de0" commit="c87070a7afc09b87ed406944b7261bfd53c3ed9c" commit_message="pygpt: Support taking path argument for LoadFromFile.  The LoadFromFile takes a file stream which is not convenient for most use cases outside pygpt. Changed to support both file stream or a string path.  BUG=chromium:834237 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I7f1f3ad009546b9aca4dfaa72c658fdea5887de0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1013450 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Youcheng Syu &lt;youcheng@chromi